#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157123 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157319 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "947c8ce4-53c5-5765-ab74-62daf58e53e1" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Graph Transformations Resulting From Reflections With Shifting"}] :question/id #uuid "437933c3-8c8b-52b8-84f0-ea6bbf789552" :question/math-academy-id "e-7516" :question/problem "The diagram below shows the function $y=f(x)$. Find the graph of $y=-f(x+3)$.\n\n![](images/8c/8c57e0ebec3c6dcc4b6d1b72a8dde395fbe4a90801c18718fc36edf84469af4f.png)" :question/worked-solution "To perform transformations of functions with multiple operations, we must remember the following rule:\n\n1. First, we perform the transformations *inside* the argument of $f$. We first carry out horizontal stretches and reflections, followed by horizontal translations.\n2. Then, we perform the transformations *outside* the argument of $f$. We first carry out vertical stretches and reflections, followed by vertical translations.\n\nTo plot\n\n$$\ny=-f(x+3)\n$$\n\nwe apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=f(x)$.\n- Translate it to the left by $3$ units $y=f(x+3)$.\n\n![](images/07/0770e092f1d63c0a9c4416f92fa6e543ffcc47bcd78375f5b835b64df3ef691a.png)\n\n- Then, reflect the result across the $x$- axis to get the graph of $y=-f(x+3)$.\n\n![](images/5f/5fde1d3543593322ad5caebbf28d4623571032e35c516dd051583294f452e679.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157198 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157378 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff702318-379a-5040-b32f-e7c89f1f2451" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Correct Order of Transformations Given a Transformed Function Expression"}] :question/id #uuid "e2417b4a-ffe8-5dc3-946e-d4c7e9a09719" :question/math-academy-id "e-8653" :question/problem "The graph of $y=-f(x-2)+3$, can be obtained from the graph of $y=f(x)$ by applying **some** of the following transformations:\n\n- $(\\textrm{T}1)$ - Translation by $3$ units up\n- $(\\textrm{T}2)$ - Reflection across the $x$-axis\n- $(\\textrm{T}3)$ - Translation by $2$ units to the right\n- $(\\textrm{T}4)$ - Translation by $2$ units to the left\n\nWhat could be a possible ordering of the appropriate transformations?" :question/worked-solution "To perform transformations of functions with multiple operations, we must remember the following rule:\n\n1. First, we perform the transformations *inside* the argument of $f$. We first carry out horizontal stretches and reflections, followed by horizontal translations.\n2. Then, we perform the transformations *outside* the argument of $f$. We first carry out vertical stretches and reflections, followed by vertical translations.\n\nTo get\n\n$$\ny=-f(x-2)+3\n$$\n\nwe could apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=f(x)$.\n- Apply transformation $(\\textrm{T}3)$: Translate $y=f(x)$ by $2$ units to the right to get the graph of $y=f(x-2)$.\n- Apply transformation $(\\textrm{T}2)$: Reflect $y=f(x-2)$ across the $x$-axis to get the graph of $y=-f(x-2)$.\n- Apply transformation $(\\textrm{T}1)$: Translate $y=-f(x-2)$ by $3$ units up to get the graph of $y=-f(x-2)+3$.\n\nTherefore, a possible order of transformations is\n\n$\\qquad$ $(\\textrm{T}3) \\to (\\textrm{T}2) \\to (\\textrm{T}1)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157199 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157379 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f0bf39b4-5615-5078-b048-99bbd7c50b50" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Graph Transformations Resulting From Reflections With Scaling"}] :question/id #uuid "86213aa7-5452-547b-9a8d-467bf870bc08" :question/math-academy-id "e-8654" :question/problem "The diagram below shows the function $y=f(x)$. Find the graph of $y=f\\left(-3x\\right)$.\n\n![](images/7a/7a0aac61b989b6aac26352c2f3faa05fc87ef37ec8ec9e120c83eabd213ed245.png)" :question/worked-solution "To perform transformations of functions with multiple operations, we must remember the following rule:\n\n1. First, we perform the transformations *inside* the argument of $f$. We first carry out horizontal stretches and reflections, followed by horizontal translations.\n2. Then, we perform the transformations *outside* the argument of $f$. We first carry out vertical stretches and reflections, followed by vertical translations.\n\nFirst, let's factor out the minus sign next to the $x$ inside the function:\n\n$$\ny=f\\left(-\\left(3x\\right)\\right)\n$$\n\nTo plot\n\n$$\ny=f\\left(-\\left(3x\\right)\\right)\n$$\n\nwe apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=f(x)$.\n- Stretch it by a scale factor of $\\dfrac{1}{3}$ parallel to the $x$-axis to get the graph of $y=f\\left(3x\\right)$.\n\n![](images/c8/c858bf111c2dbc55aa3308276d5ee93aaa0f7a0b4e5b4b69e749f552bd548d57.png)\n\n- Then, reflect it across the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=f\\left(-\\left(3x\\right)\\right)$.\n\n![](images/25/25bcd904d279c4e054e5d66b731ef294a3c1441d28e916c2824f99b9f16a3b7e.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157200 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157380 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4529c46f-0656-523f-a403-65477ea040f2" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Graph Transformations Resulting From Reflections With Other Transformations"}] :question/id #uuid "3b032f9c-3c15-5018-ae45-28b01235a3c7" :question/math-academy-id "e-8655" :question/problem "The diagram below shows the function $y=f(x)$. Find the graph of $y=3f\\left(-x+1\\right)$?\n\n![](images/ca/ca4445101ef048b82262dcca5a91d249bcf1c3172417def297ddd45cb59b9053.png)" :question/worked-solution "To perform transformations of functions with multiple operations, we must remember the following rule:\n\n1. First, we perform the transformations *inside* the argument of $f$. We first carry out horizontal stretches and reflections, followed by horizontal translations.\n2. Then, we perform the transformations *outside* the argument of $f$. We first carry out vertical stretches and reflections, followed by vertical translations.\n\nFirst, let's factor out the negative sign next to the $x$ inside the function:\n\n$$\ny=3f\\left(-(x-1)\\right)\n$$\n\nTo plot\n\n$$\ny=3f\\left(-(x-1)\\right)\n$$\n\nwe apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=f(x)$.\n- Reflect it across the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=f\\left(-x\\right)$ (remember that multiplication comes *before* subtraction in the order of operations).\n\n![](images/6c/6cde0cf55bd7a80cfb717eac89288dc99cede1b8456a0140d3e30c741958793d.png)\n\n- Then, translate the result by $1$ unit to the right to get the graph of $y=f\\left(-(x-1)\\right)$.\n\n![](images/80/803eb49b759eb31716470db93878fd2f3b73aaa0d8085bacd4be5a5f6706254d.png)\n\n- Finally, stretch the result by a scale factor of $3$ parallel to the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=3f\\left(-(x-1)\\right)$.\n\n![](images/37/3781afe1b28d36c73f2831461fee136d93a6bfe4439f47bb96dfb462a62677e2.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157629 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157378 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff702318-379a-5040-b32f-e7c89f1f2451" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Correct Order of Transformations Given a Transformed Function Expression"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ce7ca0f4-cd4b-5f35-8ad7-d652ee0e1c7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(T4) → (T1) → (T2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186154011} {:answer/id #uuid "db03b730-d113-5190-b4a8-3cc02222ef0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(T4) → (T2) → (T1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186154012} {:answer/id #uuid "f69598e0-26a5-508d-b2ad-f083510a9afd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(T1) → (T2) → (T4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186154013} {:answer/id #uuid "14cbc588-ac27-51aa-a617-5b78f43c3878" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(T3) → (T2) → (T4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186154014} {:answer/id #uuid "61bdfc50-c274-546a-9e39-59214eaa76dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(T4) → (T3) → (T2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186154015}] :answer-field/id #uuid "6fcf2f7f-47c9-5511-abd0-9f494a8dd82f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186154010}] :question/id #uuid "4695eb04-f4a4-5bc8-8cb0-35703b6e89da" :question/math-academy-id "q-17848" :question/problem "The graph of $y =-f(2x) + 4$, can be obtained from the graph of $y = f(x)$ by applying **some** of the following transformations:\n\n- $(T1)$ - Translation by $4$ units up\n- $(T2)$ - Reflection across the $x$-axis\n- $(T3)$ - Translation by $4$ units down\n- $(T4)$ - Stretch of scale factor $\\frac{1}{2}$ parallel to the $x$-axis\n\nWhich of the following could be a possible ordering of the appropriate transformations?"}]}
